ented to create benefits to as many  people as possible these include things  like  uh echo frames for example that allows  you to have artificial intelligence with  you  all the times  amazon care which is remote  telemedicine  to bring medical access to as many  people  as possible  amazon explorer which is like virtual uh  telepresence that you can go and visit  multiple places in real time  and also  in amazon globe my team is developing  computer vision to bring uh children and  their loved ones together independent of  of the distance  and a little bit of my background i  i did my undergrad degree at unam in  mexico which is a main national  university there and then i went to do  my phd in the uk and then i became a  professor  in the uk and amazon i have found this  very conductive because i i'm still a  professor in the uk but i can still  um help amazon  from from inside so i have this this  great ability of having contacts in both  academia and industry and that helps  both sides  thank you thank you  and francisco  hola my name is francisca i'm an applied  scientist at amazon i specialize in 3d  computer graphics and computer vision  i work designing algorithms to create 3d  models faster amazon we want to have 3d  models of pretty much everything we're  selling  so we need to  speed up the creation of 3d models and  that's where i work currently  before joining amazon i completed my phd  in computer science at nyu in new york  there i was working with 3d printers and  other digital manufacturing techniques  i'm originally from santiago de chile i  grew up there and did my undergrad and  master's degree in computer engineering  and then i moved to the us around 2011 i  worked as a developer in san francisco  for a couple of years before starting my  phd  so i've been in in the us for a bit of i  think 10 years and at amazon for two  years and a half already  awesome thank you francisca let's get it  started we have selected multiple  questions from the n